  "digest": "# INDUSTRIALS \u2014 2026-W44 (week to 2026-10-31)\n\n## Coverage published or changed\nTen records sit in the coverage index this week. Initiations: [ABMM](coverage/companies/ABMM.JK/report.md) ADD 2,764; [FOLK](coverage/companies/FOLK.JK/report.md) SELL 23; [TOBA](coverage/companies/TOBA.JK/report.md) SELL 304. Updates: [BNBR](coverage/companies/BNBR.JK/report.md) v2 HOLD 52; [IMJS](coverage/companies/IMJS.JK/report.md) v2 HOLD 138; [CUAN](coverage/companies/CUAN.JK/report.md) v3 SELL 323 (parked 30-Oct after two QC fails on its update); [ASII](coverage/companies/ASII.JK/report.md) v3 ADD 4,849 (was 5,006); [DSSA](coverage/companies/DSSA.JK/report.md) v6 SELL 488 (was 518); [BRPT](coverage/companies/BRPT.JK/report.md) v2 HOLD 1,111 (v1 ADD 1,411 on 30-Oct); [ADRO](coverage/companies/ADRO.JK/report.md) v4 HOLD 2,150 (was 2,327). HEAVY_EQUIPMENT, INDUSTRIAL_GOODS and INDUSTRIAL_SERVICES still have no published name (63 queued).\n\n## Deck moves\nNo INDUSTRIALS-owned deck gap. The konglo regime deck holds its 30% base holdco-discount compression and 25/50/25 scenario weights [deck S1\u2013S5]; only the HSC consequence wording was corrected on 31-Oct, with no target effect. The shared macro deck closed on 26-Oct at USD inflation 2.0%, IDR inflation 2.5% and USD/IDR PPP escalation beyond FY2029E [deck S14, S17], fixing terminal inflation in the holdco models.\n\n## Material news\nTOBA reported 9M-2026 net profit +105% yoy (IDX Channel, 30-Oct), while a companion CNBC report frames the period as a 72%-narrowed net loss of Rp641.44bn \u2014 the release needs reconciliation; the Rp7.77tn BlackRock/HPS injection (27-Oct) funds the waste platform. BNBR's 9M revenue rose 55.45% yoy to Rp4.12tn with net profit down (CNBC, 30-Oct). BRPT's 9M revenue rose 56.3% but net profit fell 66.1% on the Aster bargain-purchase base effect. OJK confirmed Rp2.1tn of fines paid by DSSA/BREN/CUAN-related parties [deck S7].\n\n## What to watch next week\nBNBR and TOBA ad-hoc updates are claimed at draft; both need the 9M release reconciled. HSC names leave the IHSG from 2-Nov [deck S3, S4], a liquidity event for BRPT, DSSA and CUAN. BRPT carries a wording fix (2.95x vs 2.54x) and awaits BREN's re-underwrite; CUAN stays parked pending its dividends restatement; ADRO's 1-Jan-2027 DSI export rule is its dated catalyst.\n\nResearch only; not a recommendation to act.",
